+{"timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:14:00Z","branch":"fixed-center finite-state invariant","note":"Finiteness reconstruction: every cyclicly labeled quadrilateral in the sequence has four vertex radii drawn from a fixed finite multiset R and four consecutive side lengths drawn from a fixed finite multiset S. Normalize O at the origin and the first vertex on the positive x-axis. Given the previous vertex, the next radius, and the intervening side length, the next vertex is an intersection of two circles, hence at most two choices. Thus each choice of four radii and four side lengths yields finitely many configurations up to rotation; since there are finitely many such choices, only finitely many congruence classes occur."}

